{"id":"fc3c1d6f4dc7038c","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-df-absolute-continuity.md","title":"Absolute Continuity","display":"df-absolute-continuity — Absolute Continuity","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-absolute-continuity","aliases":["58-df-absolute-continuity","Absolute Continuity"],"display":"df-absolute-continuity — Absolute Continuity","depends_on":["[[58-df-measure]]","[[58-df-measure-space]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-absolute-continuity"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-absolute-continuity</span><span>Absolute Continuity</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-absolute-continuity — Absolute Continuity"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"58-df-measure\">58-df-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"58-df-measure-space\">58-df-measure-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\mathcal F,\\mu,\\nu\\in V\">\\(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu,\\nu\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"58-df-measure-space\">58-df-measure-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AbsolutelyContinuousMeasure}_S,\\mathrm{MutuallySingularMeasure}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{AbsolutelyContinuousMeasure}_S,\\mathrm{MutuallySingularMeasure}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}absolute\\text{-}continuity} \\vdash \\mathrm{AbsolutelyContinuousMeasure}_S(\\nu,\\mu,X,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\land\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\nu)\\land\\forall E\\in\\mathcal F\\;(\\mu(E)=0\\to\\nu(E)=0)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}absolute\\text{-}continuity} \\vdash \\mathrm{AbsolutelyContinuousMeasure}_S(\\nu,\\mu,X,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\land\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\nu)\\land\\forall E\\in\\mathcal F\\;(\\mu(E)=0\\to\\nu(E)=0)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}mutually\\text{-}singular} \\vdash \\mathrm{MutuallySingularMeasure}_S(\\nu,\\mu,X,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\land\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\nu)\\land\\exists A\\in\\mathcal F\\;(\\nu(X\\setminus A)=0\\land\\mu(A)=0)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}mutually\\text{-}singular} \\vdash \\mathrm{MutuallySingularMeasure}_S(\\nu,\\mu,X,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\land\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\nu)\\land\\exists A\\in\\mathcal F\\;(\\nu(X\\setminus A)=0\\land\\mu(A)=0)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu \\ll \\mu\">\\(\\nu \\ll \\mu\\)</span>: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu\">\\(\\nu\\)</span> is absolutely continuous with respect to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu \\perp \\mu\">\\(\\nu \\perp \\mu\\)</span>: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu\">\\(\\nu\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> are mutually singular</li>\n<li>Under the usual <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-finiteness hypotheses, Radon--Nikodym gives a measurable <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\geq0\">\\(f\\geq0\\)</span>, unique <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span>-almost everywhere, such that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu(E)=\\int_E f\\,d\\mu\">\\(\\nu(E)=\\int_E f\\,d\\mu\\)</span> for every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\\in\\mathcal F\">\\(E\\in\\mathcal F\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Under the corresponding <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-finite hypotheses, Lebesgue decomposition gives a unique pointwise decomposition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu=\\nu_a+\\nu_s\">\\(\\nu=\\nu_a+\\nu_s\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_a\\ll\\mu\">\\(\\nu_a\\ll\\mu\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_s\\perp\\mu\">\\(\\nu_s\\perp\\mu\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Mutual absolute continuity: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu \\ll \\mu\">\\(\\nu \\ll \\mu\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu \\ll \\nu\">\\(\\mu \\ll \\nu\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Real and Complex Analysis</li>\n<li>Billingsley, Probability and Measure</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-measure","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":